+## Why
+
+The desk needs to see at a glance what can still be rented for a given period, instead of quoting or booking items one by one to find out.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `availability({ start, end, kind? })` to the rental service. It returns the ids of the equipment that is free for the whole period, sorted, restricted to `kind` when given.
+- Reuses the period rules and overlap rule of the rental service: whole-day UTC periods, half-open `[start, end)` intervals.
+- Out of scope: prices in the result, reserving anything, availability for several periods at once.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `rentals`: gains an availability query. It is expressed as an added requirement because `rentals` is still being introduced by the unarchived change `add-rental-service`.
+
+## Impact
+
+Depends on `add-rental-service` (the service, `src/rental.ts` and its period parsing do not exist yet). That change must be implemented and archived first. Touches `src/rental.ts` and `src/rental.test.ts`; no dependencies added.
